# Walkthrough - Enhanced Liquid Glass Effect

I have refined the "liquid glass" hover effect on the Benefits cards to create a more premium and interactive feel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Refined CSS Effect
Updated the `.liquid-glass` class in [globals.css](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/app/globals.css) with:
- **True Glassmorphism**: Added `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)` and a semi-transparent white background for a realistic glass look.
- **Dynamic Light Reflection**: Improved the `::before` pseudo-element with a large radial gradient that moves on hover, simulating a light source reflecting off the surface.
- **Glowing Border**: Added a subtle orange border glow (`border: 1px solid rgba(249, 115, 22, 0.4)`) and an internal white glow (`inset box-shadow`) that activates on hover.
- **Smooth Physics**: Used a custom `cubic-bezier` transition for more natural-feeling movement.

### 2. Component Integration
- Updated [Benefits.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/sections/Benefits.tsx) to remove redundant styles and allow the CSS classes to drive the visual experience.
- Improved the card layout with better padding and a more modern icon container that also reacts to the hover state.

## Verification Results

### Automated Tests
- Ran `npm run build` which completed successfully.

### Visual Audit
- The cards now have a distinct "depth" and respond beautifully to user interaction, fitting the premium aesthetic of the site.
